# The Wilds: a first walk across the land (J121.1). An island 6 km
# across, made by our own rules from one number (its seed): the coast,
# the hills, the mountains, the snow. Change the seed and it's a new island.

story The Wilds
  by: J Production
  you start in the island
  keep count of steps

colour stone: 0.5 0.5 0.48
colour dark stone: 0.3 0.3 0.31
colour bark: 0.3 0.2 0.13
colour pine: 0.11 0.26 0.17
colour dark pine: 0.08 0.19 0.13
colour oak: 0.42 0.28 0.16
colour flag red: 0.75 0.18 0.12

kind cairn
  a ball 1.6 by 0.9 m, dark stone
  a ball 1.1 by 0.7 m, 0.7 m up, stone
  a ball 0.7 by 0.5 m, 1.3 m up, dark stone
  a post 0.08 by 2.6 m, 1.6 m up, oak
  a box 0.9 by 0.04 by 0.55 m, at 0.47 3.6 0, flag red
  blocks 0.8 m

kind signpost
  a post 0.14 by 2.2 m, oak
  a box 1.2 by 0.06 by 0.3 m, at 0.4 1.8 0, turned -30, oak
  blocks 0.3 m

kind pine tree
  a post 0.4 by 1.3 m, bark
  a cone 2.8 by 2.6 m, 1 m up, pine
  a cone 2.1 by 2.3 m, 2.5 m up, dark pine
  a cone 1.3 by 1.9 m, 3.9 m up, pine
  blocks 0.5 m

place the island
  title: The Wilds
  the sky: day
  the mist: 0.00016
  the land: seed 7, 6 km across
  you come in at 0 2360, facing -20

  a signpost at 3 2350, turned 160
  a cairn called the summit cairn at -650 400
  30 pine trees between -60 2250 and 60 2340

  when you first arrive
    say: An island of our own, six kilometres across, made by rules from a single number. Nothing here was drawn by hand.
    say: The highest peak is to the north-west, about two kilometres away. There's a cairn on top.

  when you look at the signpost
    say: The arrow points north-west, up into the mountains. Someone has carved: Summit, 2 km.

  when you look at the summit cairn
    say: You stand on the top of the island. The coast runs all the way round below you, and the sea goes on for ever.
    the end: The Top of the World
